# Day 6 + Day 10 evidence: success AND failure requests for every endpoint.
# How to use: start the API (F5), then click "Send request" above any request (Visual Studio or VS Code REST Client).
# Run them top to bottom: the data is in memory, so restarting the API resets it to the 5 seeded employees.
#
# Day 10: every /api/employees request needs a token. Run the AUTH section first:
#   1. paste YOUR admin password (dotnet user-secrets list --project src/EmployeeApp.Api) into @adminPassword below.
#      It is only on your screen; DON'T commit this file with the real password in it.
#   2. run "login as Admin" and "login as User": the named requests save their tokens into {{adminToken}} / {{userToken}}.

@host = http://localhost:5286
@adminPassword = PASTE_YOUR_Auth:AdminPassword_HERE
@adminToken = {{loginAdmin.response.body.$.accessToken}}
@userToken = {{loginUser.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### ===================== AUTH (Day 10) =====================

### 201 Created: sign up a normal account (role "User": read-only)
POST {{host}}/api/auth/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "priya@example.com",
  "password": "Secret123"
}

### 409 Conflict: the same email again (case doesn't matter)
POST {{host}}/api/auth/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "PRIYA@example.com",
  "password": "Secret123"
}

### 400 Bad Request: weak password (no digit) and invalid email
POST {{host}}/api/auth/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "not-an-email",
  "password": "password"
}

### 200 OK: log in as the User. The token is saved as {{userToken}}.
# @name loginUser
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "priya@example.com",
  "password": "Secret123"
}

### 200 OK: log in as the Admin. The token is saved as {{adminToken}}.
# @name loginAdmin
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@employeeapp.local",
  "password": "{{adminPassword}}"
}

### 401 Unauthorized: wrong password (same message as an unknown email, on purpose)
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "priya@example.com",
  "password": "Wrong1234"
}

### 200 OK: who am I? (reads the claims from the token)
GET {{host}}/api/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

### 401 Unauthorized: no token at all
GET {{host}}/api/employees

### 401 Unauthorized: a made-up token (the signature check fails)
GET {{host}}/api/employees
Authorization: Bearer eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9.eyJzdWIiOiIxIiwicm9sZSI6IkFkbWluIn0.fake-signature

### 403 Forbidden: a User may read, but not hire
POST {{host}}/api/employees
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Divya",
  "departmentCode": "ENG",
  "monthlySalary": 70000
}

### 200 OK: a User may read
GET {{host}}/api/employees
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

# From here on, every request uses the Admin token.

### ===================== GET (read) =====================

### 200 OK: list all employees
GET {{host}}/api/employees
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Accept: application/json

### 200 OK: one department (query string, case doesn't matter)
GET {{host}}/api/employees?department=eng
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 400 Bad Request: department doesn't exist
GET {{host}}/api/employees?department=XYZ
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 200 OK: one employee
GET {{host}}/api/employees/2
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 404 Not Found: no employee 99
GET {{host}}/api/employees/99
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 404 Not Found: "abc" doesn't match the {id:int} route constraint
GET {{host}}/api/employees/abc
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### ===================== POST (create) =====================

### 201 Created: new employee gets Id 6, Location header = /api/employees/6
POST {{host}}/api/employees
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Divya",
  "departmentCode": "eng",
  "monthlySalary": 85000,
  "role": "Manager",
  "location": "Remote",
  "managerId": 1,
  "email": "divya@example.com"
}

### 400 Bad Request: [ApiController] automatic validation (empty name, negative salary, bad email)
POST {{host}}/api/employees
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "",
  "departmentCode": "ENG",
  "monthlySalary": -5,
  "email": "not-an-email"
}

### 400 Bad Request: business rule from Core (intern salary over 50,000)
POST {{host}}/api/employees
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Tia",
  "departmentCode": "ENG",
  "monthlySalary": 60000,
  "role": "Intern"
}

### 400 Bad Request: manager 99 doesn't exist (a mistake in the BODY, so 400, not 404)
POST {{host}}/api/employees
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Tia",
  "departmentCode": "ENG",
  "monthlySalary": 30000,
  "managerId": 99
}

### 400 Bad Request: role must be text ("Manager"), not a number
POST {{host}}/api/employees
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Tia",
  "departmentCode": "ENG",
  "monthlySalary": 30000,
  "role": 7
}

### ===================== PUT (replace) =====================

### 204 No Content: replace employee 6 (role and department change too)
PUT {{host}}/api/employees/6
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Divya K",
  "departmentCode": "SALES",
  "monthlySalary": 95000,
  "role": "FullTime"
}

### 200 OK: check the change
GET {{host}}/api/employees/6
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 404 Not Found: no employee 99 to replace
PUT {{host}}/api/employees/99
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Nobody",
  "departmentCode": "ENG",
  "monthlySalary": 1000
}

### 400 Bad Request: an employee can't be their own manager
PUT {{host}}/api/employees/6
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Divya K",
  "departmentCode": "SALES",
  "monthlySalary": 95000,
  "managerId": 6
}

### ===================== DELETE =====================

### 409 Conflict: Ravi (1) still manages Priya and Arun
DELETE {{host}}/api/employees/1
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 204 No Content: delete employee 6
DELETE {{host}}/api/employees/6
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 404 Not Found: employee 6 is already gone (run the line above first)
DELETE {{host}}/api/employees/6
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
